## 11. Important Things to Remember

- The method of pulling out a particular element from a string is called subscripting.
- Python also has negative indices. -1 refers to the last character in the string.
- Number system also works in Python, but instead of commas we can use underscore.
- Type Error: if we mismatch data types. eg: len() function takes string as argument. If we give len() argument integer, it will give a Type Error.
- len() function gives int as output.
- Value Error comes if we give invalid literal.
- input() always returns a STRING.
- Implicit Type Casting: Python is implicitly converting the result. Division always give float as an answer. 
- Python follows mathematical order of operations PEMDAS. Same priority will then occur from left to right. 
- Type convert any float to int, give floor value. 
- int() does not perform floor rounding. It removes the decimal portion (truncates toward zero).
    int(5.9)    # 5
    int(5.1)    # 5
    int(-5.9)   # -5

